CASE Statement in SQL

The CASE statement is used to apply conditional logic in SQL, similar to if–else statements in programming.

It allows you to create new values based on conditions.

# Basic Syntax
SELECT 
    column_name,
    CASE 
        WHEN condition1 THEN result1
        WHEN condition2 THEN result2
        ELSE result3
    END AS new_column
FROM table_name;

Explanation:

🔹WHEN → condition to check

🔹THEN → value returned if condition is true

🔹ELSE → value returned if no conditions match

🔹END → closes the CASE statement
